@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-targeted-authoring
A normal V2 build or play MUST NOT prepare, generate, import, resave or cook content. It validates, compiles
and checks committed packages. Preparation and import run only when explicitly asked, for the selected assets
and their declared dependents, through each asset's recorded route. An unchanged input MUST NOT launch Blender
or an Unreal import, and a no-op run MUST NOT rewrite any tracked file. Missing or stale content MUST fail with
the exact problem and its owner route, never be fixed silently, stamped as current or regenerated wholesale.
External and AI-generated sources are committed, pinned inputs recorded through atelier.ai.ledger.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-single-writer
Every committed V2 package MUST have exactly one owning record: an asset's asset.toml output or a region's
actors.verified.json. Only that owner's route writes it: a generated package only through its importer, an
editor-owned package only through a claimed editor save and its save validation. A protected write MUST hold
an active claim covering the package's scope and path, and the LFS lock that claim recorded; a task's
changed-file set MUST stay inside its claim, including companions, deletions and moves between regions.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:security] yorimichi-v2-portable-records
Asset, region and verification records MUST be portable: repository-relative paths, hashes, engine identity
and versions only, never absolute paths, hostnames, user names or times used as evidence. Package bytes
committed to Git LFS MUST NOT carry absolute donor or home paths in their import metadata; the repository is
public and LFS is not private storage. Asset licenses and redistribution rights MUST be settled before bytes
are uploaded.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] yorimichi-v2-joins-checked
Editor-authored joins between saved actors (stairs, paving, decks, region borders) MUST be accepted by an
automated gap and overlap check over the saved actors, in addition to the inherited ground, seam, closure and
walkability rules.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] yorimichi-v2-excluded-features
V2 MUST NOT load, register or link phone streaming (PixelStreaming2, AtelierStream, touch pages) or go-kart
driving (the Driving plugin, kart assets, kart UI). Shared input, audio, menu and travel code stays when an
included feature uses it; an excluded dependency is removed cleanly, leaving no missing class, asset load or
dead menu entry. V2 runtime code MUST NOT import or load files from games/yorimichi.
